        {
          "id": "momentum_numeric",
          "description": "Instantaneous numeric pin (time span 0 to 0, rel 1e-11) of the momentum rule chain on the 5x5x1 basin. STATE: u(i,j) = 0.1*sin(1.3i + 0.7j) and v(i,j) = 0.08*cos(0.9i - 1.1j) rounded to 3 decimals, 0 on the east/north wall faces; h = 100 + 7i - 3j m with a 5 m bump at (3,3); cell widths dxT by i = (10, 11, 9, 12, 10) km and dyT by j = (10, 9.5, 10.5, 11, 9) km, the face metrics and areas derived from them (dxCu, dyCv the face-centred spacings, Area_h = dxT*dyT, areaCu = dxCu*dyT, areaCv = dxT*dyCv, IareaBu = 1/(dxCu*dyCv), Aq = MOM6's Area_q, the sum of the four adjacent ocean Area_h); f = 1e-4 + 2e-6 j; uh = u*dyT*(60 + 4j) and vh = v*dxT*(55 + 3i) (face thicknesses different from the cell means, as a PPM face thickness is), with uh(2,3) and vh(3,3) scaled by 4 and 6 so that the bound_Coriolis clamp is ACTIVE at the interior faces CAu(2,3) (pvf_u above max fv) and CAv(2,3) (pvf_v above max fu); the PGF fields are smooth linear profiles. WALLS: the south-row u-faces (j = 1: pvf_u/CAu(1,1), (2,1), (4,1)) and west-column v-faces (i = 1: pvf_v/CAv(1,1), (1,3), (1,4)) are real interior faces next to a wall; MOM6 drops the wall q-point term there (zero wall fluxes) and includes 0 in the bound_Coriolis range (zero wall velocities). The pre-fix rules (which copied the edge cell into the wall slots) give twice the pvf at every such face and clamp CAu(1,1), CAu(4,1), CAv(1,1), CAv(1,3), CAv(1,4) to a nonzero bound, so these assertions fail on them. KE(1,j), KE(i,1), KE(1,1) pin avg_cell's west/south wall terms. EXPECTED VALUES come from an independent numpy transcription of MOM_CoriolisAdv.F90 CorAdCalc (dvdx/dudy :357-358, hArea_u/v :361-366, free-slip rel_vort :526, hArea_q/Ih_q/q :541-545, SADOURNY75_ENERGY CAu/CAv :724-726/:951-953, bound_Coriolis :897-908/:1139-1150, -KEx/-KEy :912-914/:1154-1156; gradKE KE_ARAKAWA :1295-1298 and KEx/KEy :1404/:1409) and of the PressureForce_FV_Bouss face law (MOM_PressureForce_FV.F90:1796-1813), evaluated on the basin padded with land cells (mask2dT = 0, Area_h = 0, zero velocities and fluxes on every wall and land face). The tolerance covers association-order differences only (e.g. the rule's 0.25*((...)*IdxCu) against the Fortran's (0.25*(...))*IdxCu).",
